{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_fault_f66_2_gate_against_rounded_reference_f66_2", "label": "Fault F66.2 \u2014 PD-0 was specified against a rounded reference and cannot pass", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F66.2-GATE-AGAINST-ROUNDED-REFERENCE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f66_2_gate_against_rounded_reference_pd_0", "label": "PD-0 \u2014 the T-D inertness gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F66.2-GATE-AGAINST-ROUNDED-REFERENCE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f66_2_gate_against_rounded_reference_storage_quantisation", "label": "Storage rounding bounds any tolerance a gate can demand", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F66.2-GATE-AGAINST-ROUNDED-REFERENCE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A reference stored at five decimals is quantised at 1e-5, so rounding alone admits |d| up to 5e-6 and a 3e-6 tolerance is unsatisfiable by any correct instrument much of the time. The 3e-6 came from s42's own one-significant-figure statement of the SAME discrepancy \u2014 the gate was set at the value it was meant to admit. The physics gate passed and the arithmetic gate as written could not; the sealed prediction is not rewritten, and the replacement PD-0' is filed with its own sha while the failure stands in the record."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_fault_f66_2_gate_against_rounded_reference_f66_2", "target": "recovered_fault_f66_2_gate_against_rounded_reference_pd_0", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F66.2-GATE-AGAINST-ROUNDED-REFERENCE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_fault_f66_2_gate_against_rounded_ref